Retried PR delivery now adopts the open PR an earlier attempt already opened instead of failing on a second `gh pr create`.

- `src/server/reviewService.ts`: imports `findOpenPullRequest` from `./github` and, in `deliverPullRequest` right after a successful `pushBranch` and before the `draft`/`createPullRequest` block, looks for an open PR for `run.branch` against `baseBranch`; when found it calls `completeApproval` with `{ delivery: "pr", grantedBy, draft: existing.pr.isDraft, prUrl, alreadyOpen: true }` and returns `{ ok: true }`. A failed lookup (`ok: false`) falls through to `createPullRequest` unchanged — never toward a merge — and the code that follows is byte-for-byte identical.
- Why: an attempt that died after `gh pr create` succeeded leaves the card in `needs_attention` with a live PR on GitHub; the retry re-ran `gh pr create`, which errors with "a pull request for branch ... already exists", so the card could never land in `done`.
